  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  name: jimtcl\n  version: \"0.84\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name|lower }}\n  version: \"${{ version }}\"\n\nsource:\n  - url: https://github.com/msteveb/jimtcl/archive/refs/tags/${{ version }}.tar.gz\n    sha256: 435095b436b38b96dd85e8cda13878144813bf52066057f76368db178dd8fea2\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - if: unix\n      then:\n        - make\n        - pkg-config\n    - if: win\n      then:\n        - m2w64-make\n        - ${{ compiler('m2w64-toolchain') }}\n        - m2w64-pkg-config\n        - m2w64-openssl\n        - m2w64-zlib\n        - m2-bash\n        - m2-sed\n  host:\n    - if: unix\n      then:\n        - openssl\n        - zlib\n    - if: win\n      then:\n        - m2w64-openssl\n        - m2w64-zlib\n  run:\n    - if: win\n      then:\n        - m2w64-openssl\n        - m2w64-zlib\n\ntests:\n  - files:\n      recipe:\n        - run-tests.sh\n      source:\n        - tests/\n        - tcltest.tcl\n        - tclcompat.tcl\n    script:\n      - jimsh --version\n      - bash run-tests.sh\n\nabout:\n  summary: A small footprint implementation of the Tcl programming language\n  description: |\n    Jim is an opensource small-footprint implementation of the Tcl programming\n    language. It implements a large subset of Tcl and adds new features like\n    references with garbage collection, closures, built-in Object Oriented\n    Programming system, Functional Programming commands, first-class arrays and\n    UTF-8 support. All this with a binary size of about 100-200kB (depending\n    upon selected options).\n  license: BSD-2-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  homepage: https://jim.tcl.tk/index.html/doc/www/www/\n  repository: https://github.com/msteveb/jimtcl\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - mdekstrand\n",
